---
source: src/ui/chat/screens.rs
assertion_line: 296
expression: "committed(help, 100)"
---
> /help
commands
/help                     commands and keyboard shortcuts
/status                   the run tree, same output as swamp trace
/accounts                 the account pool, health and spend
/usage [--json]           per-account tokens and quota windows
/trace [node]             the run tree with its events
/cost                     tokens and spend for this run
/tier [low|mid|high]      show or set the default dispatch tier
/cancel <node|all>        stop one worker or all of them
/diff <node>              the stat of a worker's captured patch
/thinking [on|off]        show or hide the brain's thinking
/clear                    clear the screen, keep the conversation
/resume <run|last>        the command that reopens a run
/quit                     leave the chat

enter         send                           ctrl+o    expand the last result
alt+enter     newline (also shift+enter)     ctrl+l    clear the screen
esc           interrupt the turn             ctrl+c    clear input, twice to quit
esc esc       cancel running workers         ctrl+d    quit
↑ ↓           history (empty input)          /         commands

shift+enter needs a terminal that speaks the kitty keyboard protocol;
alt+enter and a trailing backslash always work.
